# TerminalQ

Bloomberg-style financial terminal for portfolio intelligence, built as a Claude Code MCP plugin.

## Quick Start

```bash
./setup.sh                  # Install deps, create ~/.terminalq/, check API keys
/tq-setup                   # Interactive onboarding — obtain and configure API keys
```

**First time?** Run `./setup.sh` first to install dependencies, then run `/tq-setup` inside Claude Code for guided API key configuration.

## Private Data Storage

**Your personal financial data is stored in `~/.terminalq/` — outside the git repo and never committed.**

```
~/.terminalq/                          <-- YOUR private data (gitignored, local only)
  portfolio-holdings.md                   Portfolio positions by account
  rsu-schedule.md                         RSU vesting schedule
  accounts.md                             Account inventory
  watchlist.md                            Symbols you track
  etf-classifications.md                  ETF-to-asset-class mapping
```

- Run `./setup.sh` to create `~/.terminalq/` with starter templates
- Run `/tq-ingest holdings` to import brokerage data interactively
- The repo's `reference/` directory contains only `.example.md` templates
- `PORTFOLIO_DIR` env var can override the data location if needed

## Architecture

- **MCP Server**: `src/terminalq/server.py` — 84 FastMCP tools, JSON over stdio
- **Providers** (`src/terminalq/providers/`):
  - `finnhub.py` — Quotes, profiles, news, earnings, analyst ratings, economic calendar (60 req/min)
  - `historical.py` — Historical OHLCV, dividends (Yahoo Finance via yfinance)
  - `edgar.py` — Financial statements, SEC filings, insider transactions (Form 4), 13F holdings (EDGAR XBRL, 10 req/sec)
  - `fred.py` — Economic indicators, macro dashboard, forex rates, net liquidity, real yields & breakevens (FRED API, 120 req/min)
  - `technical.py` — SMA, EMA, RSI, MACD, Bollinger, ATR (computed)
  - `screener.py` — S&P 500 stock screener (cached CSV + profiles)
  - `coingecko.py` — Cryptocurrency prices (CoinGecko, free, 30 req/min, 429 backoff)
  - `defillama.py` — DeFi TVL across chains + stablecoin supply (DefiLlama, free, no key)
  - `cftc.py` — Commitment of Traders futures positioning (CFTC Socrata API, free, no key)
  - `etf_flows.py` — Daily spot Bitcoin ETF flows (Farside Investors scrape, free, no key)
  - `fed_calendar.py` — FOMC meeting dates (federalreserve.gov scrape, free, no key)
  - `fred.py` also exposes `get_release_calendar` — upcoming high-impact US releases (CPI/NFP/PCE/GDP/PPI/retail/JOLTS) from FRED's official schedule; the economic-calendar tool falls back to FRED releases + FOMC dates when Finnhub's premium calendar 403s
  - `mempool.py` — BTC mempool fees & congestion (mempool.space, free, no key)
  - `climate.py` — commodity-production weather/climate risk watch (NASA POWER, free, no key) + a real historical super-El-Nino stress backtest (Yahoo Finance) for the linked tickers
  - `stress_backtest.py` — generalized metric stress-period backtest (Phase 1: VIX, high-yield credit, CPI) — real historical price moves when a metric crossed its warning threshold, registry designed to extend to more metrics
  - `retail_sentiment.py` — AAII weekly survey (scrape) + SPY options put/call ratio (Yahoo)
  - `market_data.py` — yfinance dashboards: market overview, style box, fed funds futures path, equity sentiment
  - `cycle.py` — Business-cycle & recession dashboard: Sahm rule, yield curves, claims trend, NFCI, GDPNow (FRED)
  - `sectors.py` — Sector rotation: 11 SPDR sector ETFs vs SPY, cyclical-vs-defensive spread (Yahoo, free)
  - `valuation.py` — Shiller CAPE + earnings yield (multpl.com scrape) + equity risk premium vs 10y (FRED)
  - `search.py` — Web search: DuckDuckGo default (keyless), Brave Search upgrade when key set, auto-fallback
  - `portfolio.py` — Portfolio/watchlist parser (reads from `~/.terminalq/`)
- **Analytics** (`src/terminalq/analytics/`):
  - `risk.py` — Sharpe, Sortino, max drawdown, VaR, beta vs SPY
  - `allocation.py` — Asset class breakdown, concentration risk
  - `correlation.py` — Cross-asset correlation matrix (equities, bonds, commodities, dollar, crypto)
  - `correlation_regime.py` — Recent-vs-baseline correlation shift (diversification-fails monitor)
  - `percentiles.py` — Historical percentile context: ranks any metric vs its full history
  - `regime_history.py` — Regime-score calibration: realized forward returns by score band (reads the snapshot store)
  - `prediction_grader.py` — Settles due predictions in the ledger against actual prices
  - `backtest_utils.py` — shared historical-window ticker-return helper (Yahoo Finance) used by both climate.py and stress_backtest.py stress backtests
  - `fred_archive.py` — permanent local archive of FRED series history under `~/.terminalq/history/fred_archive/`; every `get_series_history` call merges live data into it so a future vendor-license restriction (like the 2026 ICE BofA credit-spread one — see below) can't erase history already banked
- **Charts**: `src/terminalq/charts.py` — Sparklines, line/candlestick charts, heatmaps, allocation bars
- **Report intelligence**: `history.py` (append-only snapshot + prediction store under `~/.terminalq/history/`), `backfill.py` (best-effort seed from existing reports); providers `reports.py` (recent-report loader) and `event_scenarios.py` (reaction-function scaffolding)
- **Infrastructure**: `cache.py`, `rate_limiter.py`, `logging_config.py`, `config.py`
- **Commands**: `commands/` — 36 slash commands
- **Tests**: `tests/` — 496 tests (pytest)
- **Docs**: `docs/` — API reference, provider/command guides, config reference

## API Keys

| Key | Required | Free Tier | Env Variable |
|-----|----------|-----------|-------------|
| Finnhub | Yes | 60 calls/min | `FINNHUB_API_KEY` |
| FRED | Yes | 120 calls/min | `FRED_API_KEY` |
| Brave Search | Optional (DuckDuckGo used when unset) | 2000 calls/mo | `BRAVE_API_KEY` |
| DuckDuckGo | No key needed | Via ddgs package | -- |
| SEC EDGAR | No key needed | User-Agent header | `SEC_USER_AGENT` |
| Yahoo Finance | No key needed | Via yfinance | -- |
| CoinGecko | No key needed | 30 calls/min | -- |
| DefiLlama | No key needed | 30 calls/min | -- |
| CFTC | No key needed | Unauthenticated Socrata API | -- |
| Farside | No key needed | HTML scrape (graceful failure if blocked) | -- |

Keys are loaded from `~/.env` via python-dotenv (`override=True`).

## MCP Tools (81)

**Quotes & Market Data:**
- `terminalq_get_quote(symbol)` — Real-time quote
- `terminalq_get_quotes_batch(symbols)` — Parallel batch quotes
- `terminalq_get_historical(symbol, period, interval)` — OHLCV price data
- `terminalq_get_dividends(symbol, years)` — Dividend history + yield

**Portfolio:**
- `terminalq_get_portfolio()` — Static holdings from `~/.terminalq/portfolio-holdings.md`
- `terminalq_get_portfolio_live()` — Holdings with live prices + daily P&L
- `terminalq_get_rsu_schedule()` — RSU vesting schedule from `~/.terminalq/rsu-schedule.md`
- `terminalq_get_watchlist()` — Watchlist with live quotes
- `terminalq_get_risk_metrics(period)` — Sharpe, Sortino, VaR, beta, max drawdown
- `terminalq_get_allocation()` — Asset class breakdown + concentration risk

**Research & Fundamentals:**
- `terminalq_get_company_profile(symbol)` — Company overview
- `terminalq_get_news(symbol, days)` — Company news
- `terminalq_get_earnings(symbol)` — EPS history + estimates
- `terminalq_get_analyst_ratings(symbol)` — Buy/Hold/Sell consensus + price targets
- `terminalq_get_financials(symbol, statement, periods)` — SEC financial statements
- `terminalq_get_filings(symbol, filing_type, limit)` — SEC filing search
- `terminalq_get_technicals(symbol)` — SMA/EMA/RSI/MACD/Bollinger/ATR
- `terminalq_get_insider_transactions(symbol, limit)` — SEC Form 4 insider buys/sells + net summary
- `terminalq_get_13f_holdings(institution, limit)` — Latest 13F top holdings for a tracked institution (berkshire, bridgewater, scion, ark, pershing_square)

**Charts & Visualization:**
- `terminalq_chart_price(symbol, period, chart_type)` — Line or candlestick chart
- `terminalq_chart_comparison(symbols, period)` — Multi-symbol % return overlay
- `terminalq_chart_allocation()` — Portfolio allocation bar chart
- `terminalq_chart_yield_curve()` — US Treasury yield curve
- `terminalq_chart_sector_heatmap()` — S&P 500 sector performance

**Economics, Crypto & Search:**
- `terminalq_get_economic_indicator(indicator, limit)` — FRED data (gdp, cpi, fed_funds, etc.)
- `terminalq_get_macro_dashboard()` — 11 key economic indicators
- `terminalq_get_forex(pair)` — Currency exchange rates (FRED)
- `terminalq_get_crypto(symbol)` — Cryptocurrency quote (CoinGecko)
- `terminalq_get_crypto_batch(symbols)` — Batch crypto quotes
- `terminalq_get_economic_calendar(days)` — Upcoming economic events (Finnhub; free fallback = FRED high-impact releases + FOMC dates)
- `terminalq_screen_stocks(sector, min_market_cap, max_market_cap, limit)` — S&P 500 screener
- `terminalq_web_search(query, count)` — Web search (DuckDuckGo default; Brave when key set, with auto-fallback)

**Macro & Cross-Asset:**
- `terminalq_get_liquidity()` — Fed balance sheet, reverse repo, TGA — net liquidity proxy for risk-asset regime
- `terminalq_get_rates_dashboard()` — Treasury yields, real yields (TIPS), and breakeven inflation expectations
- `terminalq_get_defi_overview()` — Total DeFi TVL, top chains, and TVL trend signal (DefiLlama)
- `terminalq_get_cot_report(market)` — CFTC Commitment of Traders positioning (commercial/large-spec/small-spec, WoW change)
- `terminalq_get_correlation_matrix(symbols)` — Cross-asset correlation matrix (default: stocks/bonds/commodities/dollar/crypto)
- `terminalq_get_fed_path()` — Market-implied Fed policy path from ZQ fed funds futures (FedWatch equivalent)
- `terminalq_get_equity_sentiment()` — VIX term structure (VIX/VIX3M), CBOE SKEW, RSP/SPY breadth
- `terminalq_get_stablecoins()` — Total stablecoin supply, top stables, supply growth trend (crypto dry powder)
- `terminalq_get_btc_etf_flows(days)` — Daily spot Bitcoin ETF flows in $M (institutional demand gauge)
- `terminalq_get_cycle_position()` — Recession dashboard: Sahm rule, 10y-2y/10y-3m curves, claims trend, NFCI, GDPNow → one verdict
- `terminalq_get_sector_rotation()` — 11 sector ETFs vs SPY (1/3/6mo relative), leaders/laggards, cyclical-vs-defensive spread
- `terminalq_get_market_valuation()` — Shiller CAPE with percentile vs ~150y history, S&P earnings yield, equity risk premium
- `terminalq_get_metric_context(indicator)` — Any FRED metric ranked vs its full history (percentile, min/max/median)
- `terminalq_get_btc_mempool()` — BTC fee tiers (sat/vB), mempool backlog, congestion signal (on-chain demand gauge)
- `terminalq_get_retail_sentiment()` — AAII bullish/neutral/bearish + bull-bear spread trend; SPY put/call ratio
- `terminalq_get_prediction_markets(topic)` — Polymarket real-money event odds (keyless) — cross-check on model-implied Fed path / recession odds
- `terminalq_get_dealer_gamma(symbol)` — dealer-gamma options positioning: call/put walls, net GEX sign (free Yahoo chains, estimate)
- `terminalq_get_correlation_regime(symbols)` — recent-vs-baseline cross-asset correlation shift (diversification-fails monitor)
- `terminalq_get_rsu_tax_analysis(marginal_rate, ltcg_rate)` — RSU vest tax estimates + sell-vs-hold framing (local data; not tax advice)
- `terminalq_get_climate_risk_watch()` — weather/climate production-risk watch across commodity regions (grains, softs, copper/lithium, iron ore, Permian oil/gas); NASA POWER, free, no key
- `terminalq_get_climate_stress_backtest(period)` — real historical price moves for the climate-watch tickers during a verified past super El Nino ("el_nino_2015_16" or "el_nino_1997_98")
- `terminalq_get_metric_stress_backtest(event)` — generalized version of the above for non-climate metrics (Phase 1: VIX panic, HY credit stress, CPI surge); registry designed to extend to more metrics

**Report Intelligence (history-backed, local store at `~/.terminalq/history/`):**
- `terminalq_record_snapshot(...)` — append one FR snapshot (regime scores + headline metrics); called by the FR workflow each run
- `terminalq_get_regime_history(forward_days)` — regime-score calibration: realized forward returns grouped by score band (honest about small samples)
- `terminalq_log_prediction(claim, symbol, direction, horizon_days, baseline)` — log a dated, falsifiable call to the ledger
- `terminalq_grade_predictions()` — settle due predictions vs actual prices; running accuracy/track record
- `terminalq_load_recent_reports(n)` — key sections of recent FR reports + snapshot trend (feeds the weekly digest)
- `terminalq_get_event_scenarios(days)` — upcoming releases anchored to current readings, for pre-computing the reaction function
- `terminalq_speak(text, voice_name)` — read a briefing aloud via the Mac's built-in `say` (free, no key)

